[x] Replace podman with mkosi images and systemd sessions $Darrion, 2026-10-09: see whether podman can go entirely, so personal-os needn't carry it. Assessed from the desktop: about ten call sites (build 2, run 2, secret 3, volume 1, unshare 1, rmi 1); sessions already run as systemd units. Build: mkosi profiles in personal-os (sandbox-worker base proven, personal-os 963c931), project layers as BaseTrees= or sysext (sysext covers only /usr and /opt). Run: systemd-nspawn or systemd-run with RootImage= and private users. Secrets: systemd credentials. Volumes: bind mounts. Blocker for unprivileged use: systemd-nsresourced and systemd-mountfsd are disabled on the desktop (a host change, Darrion's call); on the dev pod, as root, none. DECIDED 2026-10-09 by Darrion (answered first; my take agreed): support unprivileged systemd sandboxes; enable systemd-nsresourced.socket and systemd-mountfsd.socket on the desktop (Darrion runs it, needs root). To verify: mountfsd may require images verity-signed with a host-trusted key for unprivileged mounts, which ties to signing-key custody; directory roots should need only nsresourced. RESULT 2026-10-09 (tested on the desktop, systemd 262, mkosi 27.1): unprivileged nspawn cannot bind a user-owned clone (mountfsd idmaps only foreign-UID-range trees, by design), and a user unit with RootDirectory= shares the host network (IPAddressDeny= is ignored in user units; the session reached a service on the host's loopback). Decided with Darrion: a static system template, system/usr/lib/systemd/system/agent@.service, started by the agents group through a polkit rule; it runs as its own agent system user, and everything per run is data in /var/lib/agent-runs/<workspace> (root link, run.env, agents/, work/, home/, layers/). Verified in a real session: credential from /etc/credstore, read-only root, loopback and LAN blocked, DNS through the resolved stub, PID namespace. Layers: ExtensionDirectories= slots layers/harness and layers/project; the release file must be named after the slot (a mismatch is skipped silently under the - prefix). layers/harness (mkosi, Overlay=yes on a base tree) ran claude and pi in a session. Needs systemd >= 257. Dependencies point toward the base: the base OS knows no project, so this repo ships its units and layers and hosts install them. Hosts: on a plain Arch host, system/PKGBUILD (local makepkg -si; decided with Darrion, the proper Arch way; pacman's systemd hooks do sysusers, tmpfiles, daemon-reload); installed on the desktop 2026-10-09 and a session passed every check from the packaged unit. On personal-os hosts, a sysext later (it makes /usr read-only while merged, which blocks pacman on a mutable desktop). Gaps found 2026-10-09 while moving platform's toolchain to a project layer: (1) a project's Containerfile ENV has no layer equivalent, so .sandbox/setup exports it (e.g. CARGO_TARGET_DIR); (2) layers are read-only, so caches written at runtime (platform's /opt/uv-cache) become .sandbox/volumes mounts; (3) a project layer must install from the base's Arch snapshot, so the base should record its snapshot for agent-run to pass as --snapshot, not each project pinning its own; (4) agent-land's gate runs in podman and becomes an agent@ session too; (5) agent-run must decide when a layer is stale (podman's layer cache did this). Proven 2026-10-09: platform's full landing gate (.sandbox/setup, then scripts/validate-pinned) passed in an agent@ session on base + harness + project layers, exit 0 in 108 s. Gap (2) is not a gap: uv falls back to a cache in the writable home. Gap (6) found: git refuses a clone owned by another user; solved with GIT_CONFIG_* in the unit. polkit 127 takes the caller's process groups, so agents membership needs a fresh login (until then, newgrp agents). Gap (7), found 2026-10-09 converting layers to sysext images: an extension image carries only /usr and /opt, but Arch packages keep config in /etc (Arch's JDK: /usr/lib/jvm/java-21-openjdk/conf -> /etc/java21-openjdk), so ROBOT fails with 'Error loading java.security file'. The same layer as a directory passed the gate; why ExtensionDirectories= differed is unconfirmed. Gap (7) solved, decided with Darrion (confext pairs): each layer ships <slot>.raw (sysext: /usr, /opt) and <slot>-etc.raw (confext: /etc). Recipe, proven 2026-10-09: mkosi builds the layer once as Format=directory with Overlay=yes on the base, its mkosi.extra carrying both release files (usr/lib/extension-release.d/extension-release.<slot>, etc/extension-release.d/extension-release.<slot>-etc, ID=_any); then systemd-repart cuts both images with mkosi's own sysext-unsigned and confext-unsigned definitions (7 s), run under unshare -r with TMPDIR on a disk (not the /tmp tmpfs, which has a per-user quota). Platform's full gate passed on base + harness.raw + project.raw + project-etc.raw (27 s warm, no password prompt). The build belongs in agent-run's layer step, with staleness; layers/harness still builds Format=sysext directly until then. Format decided (meta-analysis DECISIONS 6e43036): our images and layers are DDIs (sysext), OCI only for pulling others' images; layers move from directories to mkosi sysext images and ExtensionImages=. Next: then agent-run writes run directories instead of Quadlet units; this charter's Containerfile principle and dependency table change when that lands. Step B, 2026-10-09: the project layer is optional (31edc86); a real session in this repo ran on base + harness only. Part 1 landed 41ddb67: bin/agent-layer builds a layer pair on the base when stale (recipe, base, slot, missing image, older than a week), stamps release files with the base's ID and SYSEXT_LEVEL (systemd refuses a mismatch loudly, even under '-', verified), reuses one tools tree per base snapshot (75 s first build, 15 s after), and records packages and floated versions in <name>.build.json (decision: meta-analysis 5def325). Part 2 landed bd6a8f4: agent-run and agent-land's gate make layers current (harness from the tool, project from the real repo's committed .sandbox/layer at the workspace base, via git archive), hold shared flocks from record capture to unit start, and record layers per session and gate. Proven on the host: auto harness build, platform layer from its committed recipe (166 packages, all tools), offline age-only rebuild keeps the old layer, concurrent builds build once. Hand-built layers removed. Remaining: platform drops its static release files and writes usr/share/agent-layer/versions; old snapshots' tools trees are not cleaned up.$ !3 ^2026-10-09T01:23 %2026-10-09T16:13 #01a11fc2-f801-70e1-9d36-1bad0f375602
[x] Harden host git against agent-written repository config $Found 2026-10-09 auditing the systemd runtime: the agent can write work/.git/config (and hooks) in its clone, and some config keys run commands when the host runs git there (core.fsmonitor, core.hooksPath, filters on checkout). True under Podman too (the agent ran as the person). Every host git call on a workspace clone should neutralize repository config that executes (e.g. -c core.fsmonitor= -c core.hooksPath=/dev/null, no checkout of agent-controlled attributes), or fetch from the clone into a host-owned repository and work there. Needs a test that plants such config and proves the host never runs it. CONFIRMED 2026-10-09 on the host: agent-run and agent-harvest executed repository hooks and config planted in a clone, as the host user. DECIDED (Darrion agreed): no key-by-key neutralising; the host never runs git in an agent-writable repo. The session exports bundles and a commits/dirty JSON from inside the sandbox; harvest fetches bundles into the real repo; land records candidate tips in the real repos before the gate and only update-refs real repos after. DONE 2026-10-09 (a356d73): sessions export bundles and a commits/dirty JSON from inside the sandbox; harvest fetches copied regular-file bundles with fsckObjects into the real repo; land checkpoints candidate tips in the real repos before the gate and only fast-forwards real repos after. Verified on the host with a git-logging shim over two full cycles. Residual: a SIGKILLed writer leaves no export (recovery: a short writer session, documented).$ !2 ^2026-10-09T13:31 %2026-10-09T19:06 #01a1225d-1458-7389-919c-274df9e1d60d
[x] Extract the sandbox into its own repo =sandbox-extract $Decided 2026-09-25 after evaluate-agent-runners: we write our own. Do after sandbox-driver-split, once the runner, harness adapters, harvest and land contain no ClearHead reference; grep for it as the check. The ClearHead driver stays on the ClearHead side. Extraction surfaces the remaining platform assumptions: the agents directory mount, the host pi paths, agent branch naming, and harvest assuming submodules. Proof of done: a run, harvest and land on a second repo that has no .clearhead directory.  ADDED 2026-09-29: harness tooling must leave the target repo's image. Today the platform Containerfile installs claude-code and pi, which a general runner cannot require of every repo; the runner adds its own harness layer over the repo's toolchain image, and owns the harness version pins there. The pending pi bump belongs to that layer: pi 0.99.1 (released 2026-09-29) has gpt-6.1-sol under the same openai-codex provider id, but 0.85.1 to 0.99.1 spans breaking changes, so bump it with a smoke run.  PREPARED 2026-09-30 after sandbox-driver-split: the runner no longer mentions ClearHead (grep leaves only two readers of pre-split records in agent-status and agent-harvest). NEEDS the human first on two points, ask before coding: port to Rust or Babashka or move the POSIX sh as is (about 900 lines, working); and the repo's name and whether platform uses it as a submodule or from PATH. Runner files to move: scripts/agent-new, agent-run, agent-result, agent-reconcile, agent-stop, agent-status, agent-harvest, agent-land, scripts/lib/agent-quadlet.sh and agent-runs.sh, both test files, agents/session, agents/models.env. Stays in platform: scripts/clearhead-work, .sandbox/, docs/overnight-runbook.md. Platform assumptions still in the runner, from reading the code: 1) every script finds the target repo as the parent of its own directory; it must become the git toplevel of the caller's cwd. 2) agent-new snapshots the target repo's agents/ directory; session and models.env must come from the tool's own install. 3) the root Containerfile installs claude-code and pi; split it into the repo's toolchain image and a harness layer the runner builds on top. 4) agent-run mounts Rust-only cache volumes agent-cargo and agent-target, and the image sets CARGO_TARGET_DIR; a repo should declare its own cache volumes under .sandbox. 5) agent-new reads the host's pi settings unconditionally, so a host without pi cannot create a workspace. 6) agent-land defaults its gate to scripts/validate-pinned and has submodule pin logic; the gate should come from the repo, and landing a repo with no submodules is unverified. 7) agent-harvest labels the root repo platform. 8) limits are fixed at 8 CPUs and 16G in agent-run and the unit renderer. Proof of done stays: a session, harvest and land on a second repo with no .clearhead directory. DECIDED 2026-09-30 with the human: move the POSIX sh as is, no port (revisit only when the sh hurts). It lives in a sibling repo of platform (~/Products/<name>), used from PATH, not as a submodule. Name: the human suggested agent-jobs; settle it when the repo is created. Sequence: after sandbox-premerge-gate and one real multi-action work run with a cross-vendor review, so the interface is exercised before it is frozen. Name settled 2026-09-30: agent-sandbox, at ~/Products/agent-sandbox. NOTE 2026-10-02: the NUC is being moved to an immutable container OS, and this desktop cannot host runs (no podman, 15 GB RAM). Bringing the NUC back up is the first portability test: log every host setup break (e.g. assumption 5, agent-new reading ~/.pi settings) as an extraction finding. Install target is user-space (~/.local/bin or similar); nothing installs into the read-only host. Planned split: in-platform sessions remove the 8 assumptions (one workspace, the stop-classification fix as session 1, 2-3 sessions grouped by file, cross-vendor review); then the human moves the files (subtree split or filter-repo, keeping history) and does the proof run on open-phealth. The sandbox cannot do the move: its only output is commits to its platform clone.  PROGRESS 2026-10-03, by hand on the desktop (podman now installed): the runner lives in platform/agent-sandbox/{bin,lib,agents,test} with its own README, the future repo's layout, used from PATH. Assumptions 1 (tools find their install as tool; agent-new clones the caller's git toplevel and records it as manifest .repo, which harvest and land read), 2 (agents/ snapshot from the install), 4 (cache volumes from the branch's .sandbox/volumes, named volumes only, prefixed agent-cache-), 5 (pi settings and volumes only when present and only for pi sessions), 6 (landing without submodules, tested), 7 (harvest names the repo) and 8 (AGENT_CPUS, AGENT_MEMORY, the host's) are done; clearhead-work uses the sandbox from PATH. Host finding: a pi settings.json without a packages key failed agent-new; fixed. Verified: all test/*.test.sh including land; the platform image builds here; a session through systemd on a throwaway second repo without .clearhead mounted its cache volume and sourced its setup (the session itself failed at pi login, as expected). Then, with the claude_token secret on this host: a Claude session (sonnet-5-5, 0.03 USD) on a throwaway repo without .clearhead committed a file, and agent-harvest and agent-land, run from outside that repo, landed it through its own .sandbox/gate. That repo's Containerfile was FROM platform-agent, so it does not test 3. Then 3, decided with the human 2026-10-03 (option A: the repo builds its image as root on any base and must provide git, jq and npm; the sandbox owns the harnesses, their pins and the uid-1000 user in agents/Containerfile, built FROM the repo's image by build_agent_image): platform's Containerfile lost its harness and user section; a throwaway repo on debian:trixie-slim with only git, jq and npm ran a Claude session, harvest and land, the commit owned by the host user. EXTRACTED 2026-10-03: git filter-repo moved the runner with its history (37 commits, old scripts/ paths mapped onto bin/, lib/, test/) to ~/Products/agent-sandbox, and this charter moved with it as the repo's root charter (platform keeps scripts/clearhead-work, .sandbox/ and the runbook, and calls the tools from PATH). INSTALL 2026-10-03, decided with the human: no install step. An install script was tried and dropped as imperative (it made undeclared state); installing is a declaration kept by whatever declares the host (this repo at a pinned revision, its bin/ on PATH, e.g. a chezmoi external plus a PATH line). The tools resolve their install through symlinks (readlink -f). agent-doctor is the read-only host check (git, jq, flock, systemctl, podman 4.4+ for Quadlet, uid 1000, subuid and subgid; notes for the claude_token secret, a non-empty pi auth.json in the agent-pi volume, lingering). Found on the way: agent-status exited 1 with no workspaces (fixed); an empty pi auth.json left by a failed session (the doctor does not count it as a login). Deployment split agreed with the human: the personal-os image provides the host prerequisites (podman is not in mini-server yet; that agent has it), the sandbox stays a user-space checkout, credentials are per host. PUBLISHED 2026-10-03 at https://github.com/ca-mantis-shrimp/agent-sandbox (public, MIT as platform). LEFT: tags so a declaration can pin a version; the proof on open-phealth, which needs its own Containerfile (Rust plus git, jq, npm) and .sandbox/; give this repo a remote. Cache volume names changed (agent-cargo, agent-target become agent-cache-cargo, agent-cache-target), so the first session on an existing host rebuilds its caches.  DONE in effect (2026-10-09 grooming): agent-sandbox is its own repository (github.com/ca-mantis-shrimp/agent-sandbox) and knows no project.$ !3 ^2026-09-25T16:13 %2026-10-09T19:43 <01a0dab3-2d95-7d53-a65e-cb88d090e1bd <01a0dab3-2e1a-79c2-a788-6901734ddadf #01a0dad8-d9ba-