[_] Automatically reconcile detached Quadlet runs =sandbox-auto-reconcile $Follow-up to landed run 20260925-215528. On the host, terminating the foreground systemctl start --wait caller left the Quadlet active with Result=success and ExecMainCode=0. The landed launcher correctly preserves the active unit and manifest; scripts/agent-status flags RECONCILE after it stops and scripts/agent-reconcile <id> is safe, idempotent manual recovery. For unattended operation, make terminal reconciliation automatic without a shell polling supervisor: use a systemd-owned completion/reaper mechanism or another bounded durable trigger. Preserve Git-only output, run isolation, no automatic mutation retry, and the explicit manual command. Acceptance: interrupt the launcher during a bounded no-model unit; the unit continues; when it exits the manifest reaches the correct terminal outcome and unit file is cleaned without operator intervention. Prove success, failure, timeout, OOM and manual stop retain accurate status; record recovery evidence in the manifest. Do not conflate this with the separate interactive model-control-channel design. Sequence first for unattended safety: systemd can outlive the launcher, but terminal manifest cleanup must not depend on an operator remembering the manual command. Preserve agent-reconcile as recovery and test a killed launcher against a real bounded unit.  NOTE 2026-09-30, after sandbox-driver-split, re-read before working: launchers no longer wait by default, and a stopped session is now finalized lazily by whoever touches the workspace next: scripts/agent-result, the next scripts/agent-run --in, and scripts/agent-harvest all call agent-reconcile, which works per session (unit agent-WORKSPACE-N, record sessions/N.json). What is left of this action is reconciliation when nobody calls anything, the systemd-owned trigger. Rewrite the acceptance steps for sessions: the unit and record names above replace the per-run ones.  CANCELLED 2026-10-09: Quadlet is gone; sessions are agent@ system units and agent-run --wait reconciles. Re-file if a detached agent@ session ever needs manual reconcile.$ !1 ^2026-09-25T22:40 %2026-10-09T19:43 #01a0dc3a-f71b-7f82-97be-829c00623a8e
[x] Classify a requested stop as stopped, not failed $Found 2026-09-30, the first real agent-stop under per-session units: stopping a running Claude session (workspace 20260930-133222, session 1) recorded outcome failed:exit:137, not stopped. classify_agent_outcome maps stop_requested=1 with Result=exit-code to failed:exit:<status>; a container killed after the stop request exits 137 (128+SIGKILL), so a requested stop reads as a failure. Decide which exit statuses after a requested stop count as stopped (143 SIGTERM, 137 SIGKILL at least), add the cases to scripts/agent-quadlet.test.sh, and check the smoke on a real session.  VERIFIED FIXED 2026-10-09 under agent@ units: agent-stop on a running session (workspace 20261009-194233) recorded state stopped, outcome stopped.$ !2 ^2026-09-30T14:29 %2026-10-09T19:43 #01a0f438-a648-76d2-8c6e-53cc613ad73b
